---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Print Packet
section: Mechanics
summary: >-
  Tick the chapters you want and print them as one document with a cover, a
  combined contents and continuous page numbering — plus the three prebuilt
  packets and the offline kit.
---
{#- The packet builder. Every chapter offered here comes out of nav.json, the
    same file the sidebar and the section card grids read, so a chapter added
    to the site is in the packet list without anybody remembering to add it —
    and test/smoke.mjs fails if a URL in this list is not a page that was built.

    The assembly is src/js/packet.js and happens in the browser, over the HTML
    that is already published: nothing here is a second copy of a chapter.
    print.css hides everything on this page but the assembled document, so
    "Print packet" prints the packet and not the form that made it. -#}
{%- set excluded = ["/mechanics/character-builder/", "/mechanics/packet/"] -%}
<div class="shell">
  {% include "partials/sidebar.njk" %}
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="packet-page" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-meta="section:Mechanics" data-autolink="off">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/mechanics/">Mechanics</a></p>
    <h1>Print Packet</h1>
    <p class="lede">{{ summary }}</p>

    <p>An event is a weekend in a field, and the rules are six printable pages. A player who
    wants Core Rules and the Combat Quick Reference and their own Domain has had to print three
    times and staple. Tick them here instead and print once.</p>

    <section class="packet-prebuilt" id="prebuilt">
      <h2>Three packets already made</h2>
      <p>Each is a link. Send it to somebody and they get the packet, not the instructions
      for building one.</p>
      <ul class="packet-prebuilt__list">
        {%- for packet in packets.packets %}
        <li class="packet-prebuilt__item">
          <h3><a href="{% if packet.page %}{{ packet.page }}{% else %}/mechanics/packet/?p={{ packet.id }}{% endif %}">{{ packet.name }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ packet.summary }}</p>
          <p class="packet-prebuilt__what">{% if packet.page %}One page, printed as it is.{% else %}{{ packet.chapters | length }} chapters.{% endif %}</p>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p data-packet-needs-js>Building a packet needs JavaScript. Without it, every chapter below
    is a link, and the six chapters marked <em>printable</em> carry their own print button.</p>

    <form class="packet-form" data-packet-form hidden>
      <h2 id="choose">Choose your chapters</h2>
      <div class="packet-bar">
        <p class="packet-bar__count" data-packet-count aria-live="polite">Nothing chosen yet.</p>
        <p class="packet-bar__actions">
          <button type="button" class="packet-button" data-packet-assemble>Assemble packet</button>
          <button type="button" class="packet-button" data-packet-print>Print packet</button>
          <button type="button" class="packet-button" data-packet-clear>Clear</button>
        </p>
      </div>
      {%- for section in nav.sections %}
      <fieldset class="packet-group">
        <legend>{{ section.title }}</legend>
        <ul class="packet-choices">
          {%- for pg in section.pages %}
            {%- if pg.nations %}
              {%- for nation in collections.nations %}
          <li class="packet-choice">
            <label><input type="checkbox" value="{{ nation.url | url }}" data-packet-chapter> {{ nation.data.title }}</label>
            <a class="packet-choice__link" href="{{ nation.url }}">read</a>
          </li>
              {%- endfor %}
            {%- elif pg.children %}
              {%- for child in pg.children %}
          <li class="packet-choice">
            <label><input type="checkbox" value="{{ child.url | url }}" data-packet-chapter> {{ child.title }}</label>
            <a class="packet-choice__link" href="{{ child.url }}">read</a>
          </li>
              {%- endfor %}
            {%- elif pg.url not in excluded %}
          <li class="packet-choice">
            <label><input type="checkbox" value="{{ pg.url | url }}" data-packet-chapter> {{ pg.title }}</label>
            <a class="packet-choice__link" href="{{ pg.url }}">read</a>
          </li>
            {%- endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </fieldset>
      {%- endfor %}
    </form>

    <section class="packet-offline" id="offline-kit">
      <h2>The offline kit</h2>
      <p>The site keeps a copy of itself on the device that opens it: every page, both
      stylesheets, the fonts and the search loader. Once that copy is on the phone in your
      pocket, Numina opens in a field with no signal. Nothing is sent anywhere and nothing is
      stored but the pages themselves.</p>
      <p class="packet-offline__status" data-offline-status aria-live="polite">Checking what this device has saved.</p>
      <p class="packet-offline__actions">
        <button type="button" class="packet-button" data-offline-check>Check for a newer build</button>
        <button type="button" class="packet-button" data-offline-update hidden>Update now</button>
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="packet-doc" data-packet-doc hidden></div>
  </main>
</div>
<script type="application/json" id="numina-packets">{{ packets.packets | packetData | jsonIsland | safe }}</script>
<script type="module" src="/js/packet.js"></script>
